{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user (via an automated cobbler orchestrator) has assigned Task ID 5529: create differential tests for `cmd/link` (srd084 R2.1, R2.2, R2.3). The deliverable is a single file `cmd/link/link_test.go` containing differential tests that compare the Go `link` binary against the `glink` GNU reference binary from Homebrew. The tests must cover: successful link creation, zero arguments, one argument, three arguments, and nonexistent source file. Tests must use `testutils.BuildBinary`, `exec.LookPath(\"glink\")` with `t.Skip`, and the `RunDiffTests` pattern.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Differential testing: Running Go binary and GNU reference binary side-by-side, comparing stdout, stderr, and exit codes\n   - `pkg/testutils.RunDiffTests` and `testutils.DiffTest` struct for test case definition\n   - `testutils.BuildBinary(t, \".\")` to compile Go binary from within module\n   - `exec.LookPath(\"glink\")` with `t.Skip` for graceful skip when reference binary unavailable\n   - `LC_ALL=C` environment set by default in the test harness\n   - The `link(2)` system call creates hard links (not symlinks)\n   - SIGPIPE handling via `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()`\n   - Critical design challenge: RunDiffTests runs both binaries sequentially in the SAME WorkDir, so file-mutating success cases cause the second binary to fail (FILE2 already exists)\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - `docs/specs/software-requirements/srd084-link.yaml`\n     - Defines requirements for the link utility\n     - R1.1-R1.4: argument handling, link(2) semantics, error handling\n     - R2.1: exit 0 on success, R2.2: exit 1 on error, R2.3: SIGPIPE handling\n     - Non-goals: no symlinks, no multiple targets, no directory handling\n   \n   - `cmd/link/main.go` (existing implementation, 72 lines)\n     - Handles --help, --version flags\n     - Validates exactly 2 arguments with specific error messages:\n       - 0 args: `\"link: missing operand\\n\"`\n       - 1 arg: `\"link: missing operand after '%s'\\n\"` \n       - 3+ args: `\"link: extra operand '%s'\\n\"`\n     - All errors followed by `\"Try 'link --help' for more information.\\n\"`\n     - Calls `syscall.Link(args[0], args[1])` for actual link creation\n     - Error format: `\"link: cannot create link '%s' to '%s': %s\\n\"` with capitalized error\n     - Has `capitalizeErr()` helper function\n     ```go\n     func main() {\n         sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()\n         args := os.Args[1:]\n         // ... flag handling, arg count validation ...\n         if err := syscall.Link(args[0], args[1]); err != nil {\n             fmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"link: cannot create link '%s' to '%s': %s\\n\", args[1], args[0], capitalizeErr(err))\n             os.Exit(1)\n         }\n     }\n     ```\n\n   - `pkg/testutils/difftest.go` (provided in project_context)\n     - `DiffTest` struct: Name, Args, Stdin, Env, WorkDir, ExitCode, Normalize, ExpectedFiles\n     - `RunDiffTests(t, goBinary, refBinary, tests)` runs each test case\n     - `runSubtest` runs Go binary then ref binary sequentially in the SAME WorkDir\n     - `buildEnv` merges test env with process env, sets LC_ALL=C\n     - Key issue: both binaries share WorkDir, so mutating operations conflict\n\n   - `cmd/link/link_test.go` — FILE TO CREATE\n     - Must contain differential tests for link utility\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - No errors encountered yet — only two files were read before the summary was requested.\n   - Key design challenge identified but not yet resolved: RunDiffTests runs both binaries in the same WorkDir sequentially, so for the success case (creating a hard link), the Go binary creates FILE2, then the ref binary tries to create the same FILE2 and fails with \"File exist